WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.930
Ping.

2
00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:04.480
Two students open the same
message at the same moment.

3
00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:07.340
Their test mark is back, and it's low.

4
00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:11.520
The first one shrugs, shuts the
laptop, and heads off to football.

5
00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:13.950
The second sits very still.

6
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.950
The room seems to dim.

7
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.670
Football's off tonight; they stay in.

8
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.060
Same news, word for word.

9
00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:25.190
So why does one person shrug it
off, while the other spirals?

10
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:27.850
In this mission, you'll
weigh up the suspects.

11
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.290
Was it the news itself?

12
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.600
The people around them?

13
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.000
Or something else?

14
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.620
Then you'll meet the
psychological explanation,

15
00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:37.750
and find out where it says
the difference comes from.

16
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.610
Your mission: explain why the same
news can hit two people so differently.
